[M1] SINGLE PLAQUETTE (SU(2), 0-dimensional matrix integral)
  (a) as a model: 0 spacetime directions => no transfer => m1, Lambda* UNDEFINED  [T]
      (T03-TOY: writing 'undefined' as 0 or >0 fabricates a verdict in either direction)
  (b) on the only spectrum present -- Laplace (-Delta_G) / Peter-Weyl tower, 0++ = class fns:
      j      :        1/2         1       3/2         2       5/2
      C2(j)  :        3/4         2      15/4         6      35/4
      gaps   :        5/4       7/4       9/4      11/4   (= j+1, strictly increasing)
      m1^2 = C2(1/2) = 3/4 = 0.750000   Lambda* = C2(1) = 2 = 2.000000   rho^2 = 8/3 = 2.666667
  M1(b) plaquette, Laplace tower     m1^2=0.750000   L*=2.000000   L*-m1^2=1.250000   I2=TRUE    [T]
      => I2 TRUE, but the axis is compactness (C2 strictly increasing, no accumulation),
         NOT dynamics: this IS 2D YM's leading order, not an independent model. [C]
  (c) 'one-mode' reading (a single level, so Lambda*=m1): that is the same statement as
      'there is no spectrum' => collapses into (a), not a counterexample. [T]

[M2] 2D YM (Migdal exact): E_R = (g^2/2) C2(R), 0++ tower {C2(R)}
      E(1/2) = 3/8 = 0.375000   E(1) = 1 = 1.000000
      operator O = chi_{1/2}+chi_1 fuses from the vacuum to R=1/2,1 => nu has 2 atoms
      (both residues nonzero since <R|chi_R'|0> != 0 for R' = R) => f1^2 = |c_1|^2 > 0
  M2 2D YM SU(2)                     m1^2=0.375000   L*=1.000000   L*-m1^2=0.625000   I2=TRUE    [T]
      rho^2 = Lambda*/m1^2 = C2(1)/C2(1/2) = 8/3 = 2.666667 EXACT  (R2 W2, reconfirmed)
      single-mode operator O = chi_{1/2}: nu = |c|^2 delta_{E(1/2)} only, so
      supp(nu - f1^2 delta) = EMPTY => Lambda* = +inf by the inf-empty convention:
      I2 holds vacuously. VOID row, not evidence. [T]
      SU(3) check: C2(f)=4/3 C2(adj)=3 => rho^2 = 9/4 = 2.250000

